          "prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept. Finished hero turnaround for 3D game reconstruction. Stylized hand-painted 3D game character art for a fast first-person roguelite shooter, targeting the readable, moderate-detail visual direction of Gunfire Reborn. Bold chunky silhouettes, slightly exaggerated proportions, broad clean faceted planes, two or three dominant color blocks, soft painted gradients and a few restrained edge accents. Simplify East-Asian fantasy motifs into recognizable medium-scale shapes. Use the chapter or character palette in the asset brief. Favor clear solid volume and consistent materials at normal gameplay distance. Matte stone, wood and cloth, restrained highlights on metal, sparse painted wear. No photorealism, micro-grain, dense tiny cracks, elaborate miniature carvings, harsh specular highlights or baked cast shadows. Even neutral lighting for reconstruction; prioritize silhouette and color coherence over surface detail.\nInput is the existing procedural ONE bear monk hero, ONLY for joint placement, pose and proportions. Rebuild a sculpted, cohesive and appealing game character with broad smooth volumes, chunky paws, readable gentle faceting. Keep head/shoulder/elbow/wrist/hip/knee/ankle levels, stance, asymmetric shoulder armour and hand pose. Remove polygon stacks, tiny spikes and modular primitive seams. No origami, Minecraft, photorealism or gritty textures.\nCharacter: massive anthropomorphic brown bear temple guardian monk, broad chest, thick limbs, strong round bear face, large round ears, large soft cream muzzle, broad dark nose, warm amber eyes and calm determined eyebrow. Deep vermilion monk robe across his LEFT shoulder (viewer right), simple broad muted gold border, dark indigo monk trousers, ochre cloth wraps and solid sandals with paws. His LEFT shoulder has a SINGLE massive integrated blue-grey faceted stone guard with simple bronze band and one large mountain emblem. Matching large stone bracers and shin guards, broad rope belt, a small number of thick wooden prayer beads round neck, and a simple substantial conical bamboo hat on back. Cloth has only a few big folds. Warm brown fur/cream, vermilion and slate blue colour families. Sculpted rounded anatomical shape under clothing. Hands empty, no gun, no spells or floating rocks.\nExactly FOUR consistent full body orthographic views in ONE wide row: FRONT / LEFT (faces image left) / BACK / RIGHT (faces image right). Four equal panels, same size and feet baseline. Same relaxed arms, wrists and legs as reference. Both hands outside body silhouette. Identical character details and shoulder asymmetry on every side. Fully transparent background, no floor, shadow, text or frame. Clean hand-painted game art with broad colour shapes.",
